      "writtenOn": "2025-03-15T00:12:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Honestly, I had put this self.hv_cfg.protection_type.isolates_memory() \u0026\u0026 !self.hv_cfg.protection_type.needs_firmware_loaded() check inside QTVM block and moved it out. I want to confirm with Philip once on the usage of this. Because in the kernel what happens is, if it has no fw or it is a qtvm, we don\u0027t allow it to set PC. Not sure if thats all i need to care about or not.\n\nWe care about the offset of the payload_entry_address in the region of that guest_mem to be 0. Thats what the code is doing, right?",
      "parentUuid": "175ab98f_517dea11",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 179,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 181,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "8697df57e227d7278e658f1a116f7181aa641bc6",
